Z||000012||RossT||02-03-2000||02:41 AM||||I have an ultra low mileage 88gt. It is not a<BR>daily driver. It sits in the gararge waiting for the muck to clear from the streets. I am looking to buy one as a daily driver, hopefully an 88 formula.  Non GTs are rather common up here. I know of 3 fieros within a couple of blocks from my house. I normally see one or two a day on the roads.  GT's are another story. every once in a while I think that I spotted one, then as I get closer, it turns out to be a Plymouth lazer or Dodge daytona, they kind of look like a GT from a distance. About a month ago I finally saw a 87gt, I was so excited, but when I got close, I found that it had Michigan plates.  So for now I have the only gt in Bismarck that I know of. I Have a friend that is doing a Lambo.... kit car.  He is using a 350<BR>chevy with nitrous on a fiero frame.  I will post pics when I get them.  I normally don't get down to se ND very much.  But I do alot of fishing and stuff in the Rapid City are.<P>Ross<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 02-03-2000).]||||reg||1
